Z||000000||RiceCooker||08-23-2001||07:09 PM||||Got into my car this morning and the brake pedal went to the floor. I have no leaks, inside or outside and there is still plenty of fluid in the resevoir. <P>Is this a master cylinder failure?<BR>Do i need to replace the whole unit?<P>I am currently reading more into replacing it (if i have to) with the 94 blazer mc. <BR>Has anyone else done this? results?<P>Thanks,<BR>Todd||||reg||13
Z||000001||starfighter007@msn.com||08-23-2001||08:47 PM||||well if you pump the brake pedal and the brake pedal comes up and stays up I would say you have air in your system and it has to blead out .If it keeps going to the floor you need a master cylinder .I would put a stock fiero master cylinder in it,Besides the fact that I do not know anything about the blazer master cylinder that you are refering to.Or any other different type other than what was designed for the car.but go into theogres cave and you might the information that you are looking for good luck||||reg||1
Z||000002||PBJ||08-23-2001||11:16 PM||||Sounds like you need a new master cylender, if your fluid level is up.  You need to replace it with the correct (fiero) master cylender.  The blazer m/c is for a "brake upgrade" with other calipers and rotors-not for stock system.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/forsalestart.jpg"> ||||reg||1
